+## Failed session setup
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; both hooks receive the same session and `onError` receives the same error object. No user-input or model-response stages run, so `afterSession` must tolerate setup that never completed, including partially allocated resources; its session argument does not signal successful setup, and a deployer must track allocations in its hooks ([validated by: reports a beforeSession failure and finishes cleanup before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
